2026-05-04 21:35:59 [@] how about shutdown?
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] Shutdown is currently abrupt – there's no graceful teardown of the listener or bot
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] connections. Here’s what happens:
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] - `exitForge()` in `relay.ts` is called on Ctrl-C or `exit` command. It kills `slopPid` (if
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] any), flushes buffers, saves history, and calls `Deno.stdin.setRaw(false)`.
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] - Port 8081 listener (`botListener`) is never explicitly closed. When the Deno process
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] exits, the OS closes the socket, but any active bot connections are dropped immediately – leading
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] to broken-read errors on the bot side.
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] - `slopConnections` Map and `receivePromises` are not iterated or closed. Hanging
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] `read()` promises will eventually reject when the socket is closed by the OS.
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] - No shutdown notification is sent to connected bots. They simply see a connection reset.
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] What a graceful shutdown could look like
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] A robust approach would:
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] 1. Set up a signal handler (SIGINT, SIGTERM) that calls a `shutdown()` function.
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] 2. Stop accepting new connections by closing `botListener`.
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] 3. Notify all connected bots (e.g., send a `{"shutdown": true}` message).
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] 4. Close each connection with `conn.close()`.
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] 5. Await pending reads/writes with a short timeout (force close after, say, 2 seconds).
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] 6. Wait for any ongoing AI relay calls to complete (or cancel them with an abort
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] controller).
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] 7. Then proceed with the normal exit sequence (flush, save history, etc.).
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] Currently, the code lacks this infrastructure. Would you like me to draft a concrete implementation
2026-05-04 21:36:15 [deepseek-v4] of graceful shutdown for the listener and connections?
