2026-05-07 17:18:27 [deepseek-v4] The shared files appear to be the core of a research tool called Slop Relay — a
2026-05-07 17:18:27 [deepseek-v4] multi-model, multi-user chat relay that interfaces with various LLM providers (OpenAI, DeepSeek,
2026-05-07 17:18:27 [deepseek-v4] Google, Anthropic) alongside a custom raw‑mode prompt handler and a Discord bot interface.
2026-05-07 17:18:27 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 17:18:27 [deepseek-v4] Key observations:
2026-05-07 17:18:27 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 17:18:27 [deepseek-v4] - Structure – The system uses a packed, tab‑indented TypeScript style. Named functions are
2026-05-07 17:18:27 [deepseek-v4] used extensively, which aligns with the stated preference.
2026-05-07 17:18:27 [deepseek-v4] - Async architecture – `Promise.race` drives the main prompt loop, interleaving stdin,
2026-05-07 17:18:27 [deepseek-v4] connection accepts, and bot messages. This is a clean pattern for a single‑threaded event loop.
2026-05-07 17:18:27 [deepseek-v4] - Unicode handling – Custom width calculations (`stringWidth`, `discordStringWidth`) and
2026-05-07 17:18:27 [deepseek-v4] grapheme segmentation for raw terminal input. Robust for emoji and wide characters.
2026-05-07 17:18:27 [deepseek-v4] - Shortcode expansion – Live replacement of `:shortcode:` sequences, useful for chat
2026-05-07 17:18:27 [deepseek-v4] environments.
2026-05-07 17:18:27 [deepseek-v4] - Tool integration – Models can call functions (`readtime`, `submitfile`,
2026-05-07 17:18:27 [deepseek-v4] `fetchfile`, `tagslop`) with recursive relay depth.
2026-05-07 17:18:27 [deepseek-v4] - Connection management – Accepts remote bot connections on port 8081, sends
2026-05-07 17:18:27 [deepseek-v4] NDJSON‑formatted messages.
2026-05-07 17:18:27 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 17:18:27 [deepseek-v4] Potential areas for refinement (if you’re open to suggestions):
2026-05-07 17:18:27 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 17:18:27 [deepseek-v4] 1. Type safety – Several `any` and implicit `unknown` types (e.g., `grokThink`,
