2026-05-07 20:10:56 [deepseek-v4] - The loop consumes one 2‑bit symbol every 4 PIO cycles (out+delay+jmp). This gives 2‑bit symbols
2026-05-07 20:10:56 [deepseek-v4] at 17.734 MHz / 4 ≈ 4.43 MHz – exactly one symbol per subcarrier cycle. However, the comment says
2026-05-07 20:10:56 [deepseek-v4] “4 cycles/bit” which is ambiguous; it actually means 4 cycles per 2‑bit symbol (i.e., one phase
2026-05-07 20:10:56 [deepseek-v4] step).
2026-05-07 20:10:56 [deepseek-v4] - The `jmp !x start [16]` adds a fixed 16‑cycle delay before each line. This could be refined to
