2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] - chroma.pio comment says `clkdiv=9.3885` → ~17.734 MHz (4× colour subcarrier).
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4]   But the actual code in `vidbit.cpp` sets `piosmset_clkdiv(pio,sm,2.3471f)`.
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4]   This gives `166.5 / 2.3471 ≈ 70.94 MHz` (16× colour subcarrier).
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4]   The chroma program’s output rate is `70.94 MHz / 4 cycles per sample = 17.735 MHz` –
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] exactly 4× f_sc, as required for PAL.
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4]   The clock divider in the code (2.3471) is correct; the comment is outdated.
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] 2. Chroma program loop and sample count
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] The chroma program outputs one 2‑bit sample (phase) every 4 PIO cycles:
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] loop:
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4]     out   pins, 2 [2]     ; 1 cycle + 2 wait
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4]     jmp   x--, loop       ; 1 cycle
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] Total 4 cycles per sample.
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] • Expected samples per active line*
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] - Active video duration: 51.904 µs
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] - Chroma sample rate: 17.735 MHz
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] - Samples = 51.904 µs × 17.735 MHz ≈ 920
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] The counter `x` must be loaded with 920 (or slightly more for burst + front/back porch? The burst
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] is generated separately? Actually burst is output during the back porch, before active video. But
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] the chroma program is triggered by IRQ 4, which is set at the start of back porch. So the `x` count
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] should cover the entire chroma burst + active video + maybe front porch? The burst is part of the
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] chroma waveform; the program outputs samples continuously until the counter expires. In PAL, the
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] burst is 10±1 cycles of subcarrier = 40 samples, then active video ≈ 920 samples, total ≈ 960
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] samples.
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] • But the initial count set in `initChroma()` is:*
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] int count = (colorWords-1)*16 - 1;   // colorWords=128 ⇒ count = 2031
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] 2031 is much larger than 960. That would produce ~230 µs of chroma, far longer than one line.
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] • Possible explanation:*
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] The chroma program uses multiple FIFO words per line (each word provides 16 samples). The
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] counter `x` might be the number of words to process, not samples. Let's examine the program
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] flow:
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] After `wait 1 irq 4` and `irq clear 4`, the program does:
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] out x, 32               ; load counter from FIFO (first word)
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] jmp !x start [16]       ; if counter=0, wait for next irq
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] loop:
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4]     out pins, 2 [2]      ; output 2 bits from OSR
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4]     jmp x--, loop        ; decrement counter
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] There is no `pull` instruction. The OSR is only loaded once from the FIFO (the first word
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] becomes `x`). After that, every `out pins, 2` shifts bits out of the OSR. With `autopull = false`
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] in the config, the OSR is never refilled from the FIFO. Therefore, after the first `out
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] pins, 2` (which uses 2 bits), the OSR still contains 30 bits. After 15 more `out pins, 2` (total 16
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] iterations, 32 bits used), the OSR is empty. Any further `out pins` will stall forever because
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] autopull is disabled.
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] This means the program as written cannot output more than 16 samples per line unless
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] `autopull` is enabled and the pull threshold matches.
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] The comment “8 bits from FIFO = 2 full color subcarrier cycles (4 bits per cycle)” suggests each
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] FIFO word was intended to hold 8 bits (4 cycles), not 32. But the code uses 32‑bit words.
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] • Conclusion:* The chroma PIO program has a fundamental bug: it lacks either:
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] - An `autopull` configuration with threshold 2 (or 32) and a `pull` instruction, or
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] - A loop that fetches a new word from FIFO after each 16 samples.
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] Without that, the chroma state machine will stall after ~16 samples and never output the full line.
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] 3. Burst phase and alignment
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] - Burst is generated by `colorWord[2]` and `colorWord[3]`, which are both set to `0x23102310`. This
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] pattern corresponds to phases 2,3,1,0 (if we map 0→00,1→01,2→10,3→11). In PAL, the colour burst
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] should be a continuous sine wave of constant phase (135° for PAL? Actually PAL burst phase
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] alternates line-to-line). The code does not alternate, and the burst pattern seems arbitrary.
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] - The burst is placed before active video, but its length is only 2 words (32 samples = 8
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] subcarrier cycles). PAL requires 10±1 cycles, so this is a bit short.
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] 4. Field alternation and colour framing
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] The DMA ring buffer has two halves (even/odd field) but the chroma program does not differentiate.
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] The colour subcarrier must be 180° out of phase on alternate lines to implement PAL’s V-switch. The
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] current buffer does not account for that – both fields use the same colour data, which would cause
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] incorrect colour on every other line.
2026-05-07 20:35:51 [deepseek-v4] 
