2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] ╭───────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] │  Aspect                   │  Current                 │  Required                                                                             │
2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] ├───────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] │  Counter per line         │  2031                    │  959 (or 960)                                                                         │
2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] │  Burst length             │  32 samples (2 words)    │  40 samples (2.5 words or pad)                                                        │
2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] │  DMA synchronisation      │  Infinite loop, no sync  │  Restart DMA per line or use a ring that exactly matches one line’s FIFO consumption  │
2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] │  FIFO alignment           │  Counter word only once  │  Ensure first word after IRQ is counter; DMA must not pre‑fill during wait            │
2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] ╰───────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] A practical fix:
2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] - Reduce `count` to 959 and adjust data buffer size accordingly.
2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] - Use a single‑shot DMA triggered by the video IRQ (or by checking that chroma DMA is
2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] busy). For each line, (re)start DMA with a transfer count of `1 + (samples/16)` words (where
2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] samples = 960, so 1+60=61 words).
2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] - Alternatively, keep the infinite ring but embed the counter word at the same offset every
2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] line. That would require the ring buffer to contain multiple copies of the line structure, one
2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] per line, with the per‑line IRQ still needed to ensure the PIO reads the correct word. This is more
2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] complex.
2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] Given the complexity, a simpler approach would be to rewrite the chroma PIO program to not use
2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] a counter word but instead rely on a fixed‑length DMA transfer that exactly fills one line’s
2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] worth of data. The PIO would loop for a fixed number of autopulls (e.g., 60 words) and then wait
2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] for the next IRQ. This eliminates the need to count.
2026-05-07 20:45:55 [deepseek-v4] 
