2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] │  PAL colour subcarrier       │  `4.43361875 MHz × 4`                                            │  `17.734475 MHz` ✅        │
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] │  Active line video duration  │  (back porch + burst + active video) ≈ `5.79 + 0.56? + 51.9 μs`  │  `~54.5 μs`               │
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] │  Required samples per line   │  `54.5 μs × 17.735 MHz`                                          │  **≈ 967 samples**        │
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] ╰──────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────╯
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] 2. Current counter and buffer size
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] - `int count = (colorWords-1)*16 - 1 = 2031` → 2031 samples per line.
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] - 2031 samples × 56.4 ns = 114.5 μs — exceeds the 64 μs PAL line by nearly a factor of two.
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] - The chroma output will overflow into the next line’s sync, corrupting the signal.
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] • Correct counter:* `967` (or 966 if zero‑indexed) → `int count = 966;`
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] 3. Burst length
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] - `burst32` provides 32 samples = 8 subcarrier cycles.
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] - PAL requires 10±1 cycles (40±4 samples).
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] - Current burst length is too short by 2 cycles (8 instead of 10).
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] • Fix:* Use 40 samples: e.g., `colorWord[1] = burst32; colorWord[2] = burst32; colorWord[3]
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] = some 8‑sample word`.
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] Alternatively, store the entire burst in the first 2.5 words and adjust the data buffer
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] accordingly.
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] 4. DMA synchronisation (critical flaw)
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] The DMA is configured with `UINT32_MAX` (infinite transfer) and a ring buffer of size `2*colorWords
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] = 256` words.
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] After the first line, the chroma PIO will:
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] - Wait for IRQ 4
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] - Read the next word from the TX FIFO as the counter
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] - Because the DMA never stops and keeps filling the FIFO, that word will not be the
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] intended counter ( `colorWord[0]` ), but a data word (e.g., `burst32` ).
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] This causes the counter to be misinterpreted (e.g., `0x23102310` interpreted as a 32‑bit counter =
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] 588,368,144 → > 1e9 samples → desync).
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] • Required change:*
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] - Use per‑line DMA re‑trigger (like `vid_field` does for video).
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] - For each line, set:
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4]   - `dmachannelsetreadaddr(chromadmachan, colorWord);` (address of counter)
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4]   - `dmachannelsettranscount(chromadmachan, 1 + 960/16);` (1 counter word +
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] 60 data words = 61 words)
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] - Restart the DMA after each IRQ, or use an interrupt when the video state machine sets IRQ 4 to
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] trigger the chroma DMA.
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] 5. V‑switch (PAL alternation)
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] The buffer contains two halves (`colorWord[0..127]` for even field? Actually
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] `colorWord[colorWords*2]` with a ring of size 256).
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] There is no alternation of burst phase or colour data between lines – PAL requires the subcarrier
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] polarity (or at least the burst phase) to be inverted on alternate lines (the V‑switch). Without
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] this, the colour information will appear as hue errors on every other line.
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] • Fix:*
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] - The buffer should contain two separate line patterns: one for even lines, one for odd lines (or
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] use the ring to switch between two buffers).
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] - The burst phase should be 180° shifted on alternate lines: e.g., use `0x3102` instead of `0x2310`
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] for the opposite phase.
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] Summary of required corrections
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] ╭──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────╮
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] │  Aspect                  │  Current              │  Required                       │
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] ├──────────────────────────┼──────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] │  Samples per line        │  2031                 │  967                            │
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] │  Burst length            │  32 samples (8 cycles)│  40 samples (10 cycles)         │
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] │  DMA mode                │  Infinite, ring       │  Single‑shot per line           │
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] │  DMA trigger             │  None (always running)│  On IRQ 4 from video PIO       │
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] │  PAL V‑switch            │  No alternation       │  Alternate burst phase + data  │
2026-05-07 20:52:41 [deepseek-v4] ╰──────────────────────────┴──────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────╯
