2026-05-11 19:54:28 [deepseek-v4] - `drawC64Char`: Uses `flipBits` to reverse bit order. The font array is stored MSB first
2026-05-11 19:54:28 [deepseek-v4] (bit 0 of byte is leftmost pixel?) Typical C64 font is LSB first (bit 0 = rightmost), but the code
2026-05-11 19:54:28 [deepseek-v4] flips bits, so it expects the opposite. Verify.
2026-05-11 19:54:28 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-11 19:54:28 [deepseek-v4] - `rect` and `erase`: Works by OR-ing bits for rect (set), or AND with mask for erase.
2026-05-11 19:54:28 [deepseek-v4] Correct.
2026-05-11 19:54:28 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-11 19:54:28 [deepseek-v4] - Use of `lineWords=27`: With line width 864, that’s 27 words (864/32 = 27 exactly). Good.
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] Suggestions for Improvement
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] 1. Fix PIO pin direction usage: Replace `set pindirs, 0/1` with `set pins, 0/1` and keep
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] the pin always output. Keep `out pindirs, 1` only if you really intend to toggle direction
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] (unlikely). Use `out pins, 1` for active video.
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] 2. Correct chroma clock divider: Change `piosmset_clkdiv(pio,sm,2.3471f)` to
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] `9.3885f` (or compute more precisely: 166.5 / (4*4.43361875) ≈ 9.3885). Also ensure the chroma PIO
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] waits for IRQ from video; either enable IRQ 4 in `vidbit.pio` or use a different sync method.
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] 3. Initialize ISR for pixel count: In `vidbit.pio`, before the line loop, load the pixel
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] counter into ISR: `mov isr, y` or `out isr, 32` after loading y from FIFO. Currently it’s using
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] `mov y, isr` without initializing ISR. That will give undefined behavior.
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] 4. Document timing: Add a comment block in `vidbit.pio` that calculates each segment:
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] HSYNC, back porch, active, front porch, and sum to 10656 cycles. Verify with actual numbers.
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] 5. Modularize frame buffer allocation: Move declarations of `evenFrame`, `oddFrame`,
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] `evenWords`, `oddWords` into a shared header (e.g., `pal576i.h`). Use `constexpr` or `#define` for
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] line counts.
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] 6. Pre‑compute teletext packets: Instead of recomputing each field, build a static teletext
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] page and only update when needed (e.g., on text input). The current per‑field rebuild is fine for a
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] demo, but might lag if the CPU is busy.
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] 7. Consider using PIO’s `irq` for field sync: Set an IRQ flag in the video PIO at the end
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] of each field (or line) to trigger the chroma PIO to start. The chroma PIO could use `wait 1 irq 4`
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] and then process the next field’s chroma data. This would eliminate the need for the main loop to
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] poll.
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] 8. Double‑buffer for chroma: The chroma DMA is set to a ring buffer; if you want
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] alternating even/odd fields, you could have two separate buffers and switch DMA reads per field,
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] similar to video.
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] 9. Remove unused code: e.g., `static uint32_t pcm32=0;` not used, `int pioStatus` assigned
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] but never checked, `bool led` global.
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] 10. Add error handling: e.g., `piocanadd_program` returns false, but code only does
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] `pass&=...` and continues. Print a diagnostic or halt.
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] Conclusion
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] This is a sophisticated project that shows excellent use of PIO and DMA on the RP2350. The main
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] issues are the pin direction confusion in `vidbit.pio` and the chroma clock divider. With those
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] fixed, the conceptual design is sound. The interlace, teletext, and chroma overlays are nice
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] features. I encourage you to keep refining and document the timing constraints.
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] If you have specific questions about any part, feel free to ask. I’m happy to help debug or suggest
2026-05-11 19:54:29 [deepseek-v4] alternative implementations.
