2026-05-11 19:58:41 [simon@midnightblue.local] i want to get ready for colorfifo testing, beginning with c setup of the fifo color palette
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] Here's a starting point for the palette setup. The key insight is that with `.fifo txget`, the TX
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] FIFO becomes addressable storage — you push palette entries via the normal `piosmput`, and
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] PIO reads them back indexed by `y`.
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] Each palette entry packs 6 cycles × 3 pindir bits = 18 bits, LSB-first (since `out` shifts low end
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] first):
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] // colorfifo palette: 4 colors × 6 cycles × 3 pindir bits per cycle
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] // pindir=1 drives line (Y/Pb/Pr GPIO held low), pindir=0 releases (Hi-Z)
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] constexpr int PALETTE_COLORS = 4;
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] constexpr int PALETTE_CYCLES = 6;
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] constexpr int PALETTE_CHANNELS = 3;
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] struct ColorEntry {
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	uint8_t cycle[PALETTE_CYCLES];	// each entry: 3 bits (b0=Y, b1=Pb, b2=Pr)
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] };
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] uint32_t encodeColorEntry(const ColorEntry &e) {
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	uint32_t w = 0;
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	for (int i = 0; i < PALETTE_CYCLES; i++) {
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 		w |= (uint32_t)(e.cycle[i] & 0x7) << (i * PALETTE_CHANNELS);
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	}
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	return w;
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] }
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] void loadColorPalette(PIO pio, int sm, const ColorEntry palette[PALETTE_COLORS]) {
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	for (int i = 0; i < PALETTE_COLORS; i++) {
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 		pio_sm_put_blocking(pio, sm, encodeColorEntry(palette[i]));
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	}
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] }
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] A trivial test palette — color 0 = black (no drive), 1 = Y only, 2 = Pb only, 3 = Pr only, each
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] pulsing 3 cycles on / 3 off so you can spot it on a scope:
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] const ColorEntry testPalette[PALETTE_COLORS] = {
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	{{ 0b000, 0b000, 0b000, 0b000, 0b000, 0b000 }},	// 0: idle
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	{{ 0b001, 0b001, 0b001, 0b000, 0b000, 0b000 }},	// 1: Y pulse
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	{{ 0b010, 0b010, 0b010, 0b000, 0b000, 0b000 }},	// 2: Pb pulse
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	{{ 0b100, 0b100, 0b100, 0b000, 0b000, 0b000 }},	// 3: Pr pulse
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] };
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] And a skeleton init that wires the SM up. The pin bases need confirming against your board — the
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] doc names GP42..45 as the per-SM wait pins and GP46/47 as the shared 2-bit colour index, but I
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] don't see the Y/Pb/Pr base spelled out for the pindir outputs (you have YPIN=17, PBPIN=18,
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] PR_PIN=19 in vidbit.cpp — assuming those):
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] constexpr uint COLOR_OUT_BASE = 17;	// Y_PIN, PB_PIN, PR_PIN consecutive
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] constexpr uint COLOR_INDEX_BASE = 46;	// 2-bit index from colorpump
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] bool colorfifo_init(PIO pio, int sm, uint wait_pin) {
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	const pio_program_t *program = &colorfifo_program;
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	if (!pio_can_add_program(pio, program)) return false;
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	uint offset = pio_add_program(pio, program);
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	for (uint i = 0; i < PALETTE_CHANNELS; i++) {
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 		pio_gpio_init(pio, COLOR_OUT_BASE + i);
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 		gpio_set_dir(COLOR_OUT_BASE + i, GPIO_IN);	// start Hi-Z
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 		gpio_put(COLOR_OUT_BASE + i, 0);		// preload low for when pindir flips
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	}
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	pio_sm_config c = colorfifo_program_get_default_config(offset);
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	sm_config_set_out_pins(&c, COLOR_OUT_BASE, PALETTE_CHANNELS);
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	sm_config_set_set_pins(&c, COLOR_OUT_BASE, PALETTE_CHANNELS);
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	sm_config_set_in_pins(&c, COLOR_INDEX_BASE);		// for mov y, pins
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	sm_config_set_jmp_pin(&c, wait_pin);			// per-SM wait line
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	sm_config_set_out_shift(&c, true, true, PALETTE_CYCLES * PALETTE_CHANNELS);
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	// .fifo txget — TX FIFO becomes indexable via rxfifo[y]
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	// (SDK 2.x: sm_config_set_fifo_join with the PUTGET variant)
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	sm_config_set_fifo_join(&c, PIO_FIFO_JOIN_PUTGET);
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	pio_sm_init(pio, sm, offset, &c);
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	loadColorPalette(pio, sm, testPalette);
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	pio_sm_set_enabled(pio, sm, true);
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 	return true;
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] }
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] A few things worth flagging before you wire this in:
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 1. The `.fifo txget` enum name varies between SDK versions — on current pico-sdk for RP2350 it's
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] `PIOFIFOJOINPUTGET`. If the pioasm-generated
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] `colorfifoprogramgetdefaultconfig` already calls it, you can drop the explicit
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] `smconfigsetfifo_join` line.
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 2. `mov osr, rxfifo[y]` — the index range is 0..3 for a 4-deep half-FIFO. If you intend more than 4
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] colours you'll need a different scheme, but the .pio reads exactly 4.
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 3. The colorfifo program has no explicit `pull` — once preloaded, the TX FIFO entries act as ROM.
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] So `loadColorPalette` is a one-shot at init. If you want runtime palette swaps, you'll need to stop
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] the SM, refill, and restart, or design a separate update path.
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 4. The `set pindirs, 0` at the end releases all 3 channels — good. But the initial pin state
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] (level=0) needs to be set before the SM enables, otherwise the first pulse may glitch. The
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] `gpioput` before `piogpioinit` ordering matters; you may want to swap, or set level via
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] `gpioset_outover` once SDIO has them.
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] Want me to sketch the colorpump-side dispatch next, or shall we get the four colorfifo SMs claimed
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] and stalled-on-jmp-pin first?
2026-05-11 19:59:31 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:00:36 [simon@midnightblue.local] there will be four concurrent colorfifo
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] Right — four SMs likely all sharing the Y/Pb/Pr output pins and the 2-bit colour index, but each
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] gated by its own wait pin (GP42..45). Since only one fifo unstalls at a time (colorpump pulses one
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] wait line), output contention isn't an issue as long as the off-duty SMs hold `pindirs=0`.
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] Refactoring to handle the set of four:
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] constexpr int COLORFIFO_COUNT = 4;
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] constexpr uint COLOR_OUT_BASE = 17;	// Y, Pb, Pr (3 consecutive)
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] constexpr uint COLOR_INDEX_BASE = 46;	// 2-bit colour selector
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] constexpr uint COLOR_WAIT_BASE = 42;	// GP42..45, one per SM
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] struct ColorFifo {
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	PIO pio;
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	uint sm;
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	uint wait_pin;
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] };
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] static ColorFifo colorFifos[COLORFIFO_COUNT];
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] static uint colorfifo_offset;
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] bool addColorfifoProgram(PIO pio) {
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	if (!pio_can_add_program(pio, &colorfifo_program)) return false;
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	colorfifo_offset = pio_add_program(pio, &colorfifo_program);
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	return true;
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] }
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] void configureColorfifoPins(PIO pio) {
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	for (uint i = 0; i < PALETTE_CHANNELS; i++) {
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 		uint pin = COLOR_OUT_BASE + i;
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 		pio_gpio_init(pio, pin);
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 		gpio_set_dir(pin, GPIO_IN);
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 		gpio_put(pin, 0);
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	}
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	for (uint i = 0; i < COLORFIFO_COUNT; i++) {
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 		uint pin = COLOR_WAIT_BASE + i;
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 		gpio_init(pin);
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 		gpio_set_dir(pin, GPIO_IN);
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 		gpio_pull_up(pin);	// idle high, colorpump pulses low to trigger
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	}
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	for (uint i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 		uint pin = COLOR_INDEX_BASE + i;
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 		gpio_init(pin);
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 		gpio_set_dir(pin, GPIO_IN);
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	}
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] }
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] bool initColorfifoSM(PIO pio, uint sm, uint wait_pin) {
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	pio_sm_config c = colorfifo_program_get_default_config(colorfifo_offset);
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	sm_config_set_out_pins(&c, COLOR_OUT_BASE, PALETTE_CHANNELS);
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	sm_config_set_set_pins(&c, COLOR_OUT_BASE, PALETTE_CHANNELS);
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	sm_config_set_in_pins(&c, COLOR_INDEX_BASE);
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	sm_config_set_jmp_pin(&c, wait_pin);
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	sm_config_set_out_shift(&c, true, true, PALETTE_CYCLES * PALETTE_CHANNELS);
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	if (pio_sm_init(pio, sm, colorfifo_offset, &c) != 0) return false;
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	loadColorPalette(pio, sm, testPalette);
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	return true;
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] }
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] bool initColorfifos(PIO pio, const ColorEntry palette[PALETTE_COLORS]) {
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	if (!addColorfifoProgram(pio)) return false;
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	configureColorfifoPins(pio);
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	for (uint i = 0; i < COLORFIFO_COUNT; i++) {
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 		int sm = pio_claim_unused_sm(pio, true);
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 		if (sm < 0) return false;
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 		colorFifos[i] = { pio, (uint)sm, COLOR_WAIT_BASE + i };
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 		if (!initColorfifoSM(pio, sm, COLOR_WAIT_BASE + i)) return false;
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 		loadColorPalette(pio, sm, palette);
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	}
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	for (uint i = 0; i < COLORFIFO_COUNT; i++) {
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 		pio_sm_set_enabled(colorFifos[i].pio, colorFifos[i].sm, true);
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	}
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 	return true;
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] }
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] A few things to think through before testing:
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] • 1. All four SMs share the same instruction memory* — `pioaddprogram` is called
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] once, all SMs reference `colorfifo_offset`. Good — saves three quarters of the program slots.
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] • 2. Palette duplication* — each SM has its own TX FIFO, so the same 4-entry palette must
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] be pushed into each of the four FIFOs separately. That's what `loadColorPalette` per-SM in the loop
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] does. Worth noting: if you ever want different palettes per SM (e.g. odd/even line variants), you
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] have that flexibility for free.
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] • 3. PIO block choice* — pio0 has vidbit+wst, pio1 has chroma+audio (i2s), pio2 has
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] keyboard. So pio2 has 3 SMs free, not enough for 4. You'll either need to consolidate (move ps2 to
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] pio1, or chroma+audio share pio0 instead) or split colorfifos across PIO blocks. Splitting is fine
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] but `pioaddprogram` and pin init must run per PIO block used.
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] • 4. Wait pin polarity — `jmp pin stall` jumps while pin is high, so colorpump must
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] pulse the wait line low* to release the SM. Your colorpump.pio's `set pins, 14` (= 0b1110)
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] pulls bit 0 low — that matches if SM0's wait pin is the LSB of colorpump's `set` group. The mapping
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] needs to line up: colorpump set base → colorfifo wait pins must be aligned.
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] • 5. Race after release* — once the wait pin goes high again (colorpump's `set pins, 15`),
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] the SM has already taken the `mov y, pins` path and is mid-burst. Six `out pindirs, 3` cycles each
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] take 1 PIO cycle, so the burst is 6 cycles + the housekeeping. As long as the colorpump's "low
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] pulse" duration exceeds 1 PIO cycle on the colorfifo's clock, the jmp will fall through reliably.
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] Worth verifying both SMs run at the same clkdiv.
2026-05-11 20:01:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
