2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] Got it — so the effective 4-bit colour word is split: 2 bits drive the shared index pins (selecting
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] within a palette), 2 bits select which of the four colorfifo SMs gets its wait pin pulsed
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] (selecting the palette). Looking at colorpump.pio that's exactly what it does: `out pins, 2` for
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] the index, then `out x, 2` decodes which of t0..t3 to fire.
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] Restructuring around a 16-entry master palette:
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] constexpr int PALETTES = 4;
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] constexpr int COLORS_PER_PALETTE = 4;
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] constexpr int TOTAL_COLORS = PALETTES * COLORS_PER_PALETTE;	// 16
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] // Master 16-colour palette; layout: palette p, index i → masterPalette[p*4 + i]
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] // Colour word from colorpump: bits[1:0]=index, bits[3:2]=palette
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] typedef ColorEntry MasterPalette[TOTAL_COLORS];
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] void loadMasterPalette(const MasterPalette &master) {
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 	for (int p = 0; p < PALETTES; p++) {
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 		const ColorFifo &cf = colorFifos[p];
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 		for (int i = 0; i < COLORS_PER_PALETTE; i++) {
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 			uint32_t w = encodeColorEntry(master[p * COLORS_PER_PALETTE + i]);
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 			pio_sm_put_blocking(cf.pio, cf.sm, w);
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 		}
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 	}
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] }
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] The init flow becomes "claim and configure four SMs with no palette loaded, then load master in one
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] pass":
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] bool initColorfifos(PIO pio, const MasterPalette &master) {
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 	if (!addColorfifoProgram(pio)) return false;
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 	configureColorfifoPins(pio);
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 	for (uint i = 0; i < COLORFIFO_COUNT; i++) {
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 		int sm = pio_claim_unused_sm(pio, true);
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 		if (sm < 0) return false;
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 		colorFifos[i] = { pio, (uint)sm, COLOR_WAIT_BASE + i };
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 		if (!initColorfifoSM(pio, (uint)sm, COLOR_WAIT_BASE + i)) return false;
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 	}
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 	loadMasterPalette(master);
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 	for (uint i = 0; i < COLORFIFO_COUNT; i++) {
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 		pio_sm_set_enabled(colorFifos[i].pio, colorFifos[i].sm, true);
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 	}
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] 	return true;
2026-05-11 20:02:36 [claude-opus-4-7] }
