2026-05-11 20:42:45 [simon@midnightblue.local] i fixed the offsets in colorpump_init and now i want to discuss settup up the 4 fifo
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] Good. Let's talk through the four colorfifo SMs.
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] From what I can see in `colorfifo.pio`:
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] - `.fifo txget` — TX FIFO is in "get" mode, meaning the CPU writes to it but the SM uses `mov osr,
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] rxfifo[y]` style indexed access rather than autopull. So you're treating it as a 4-entry indexed
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] lookup table per SM.
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] - `jmp pin stall` — gated by one of the four PUMP_ENABLE pins (GP2..GP5).
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] - `mov y, pins` reads the 2-bit color index (GP0..GP1, the COLOR_I pins shared by all four fifos).
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] - `mov osr, rxfifo[y]` indexes one of 4 preloaded words.
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] - Six `out pindirs, 3` instructions consume 18 bits of OSR, driving a 3-pin pindirs pulse train
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] over 6 cycles.
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] - `set pindirs, 0` releases all three pins to Hi-Z.
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] So each of the 4 SMs needs:
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 1. Its own JMP pin mapped to one of PUMP0..PUMP3_ENABLE (GP2..GP5). This is what
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] differentiates the four SMs.
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 2. Shared IN base at COLOR_I0 (GP0), 2 pins, to read the color index.
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 3. Shared SET/OUT base at the 3 output pins (Y/PB/PR = GP17..GP19), 3 pins wide,
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] controlling pindirs.
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 4. Four words preloaded into its TX FIFO at startup — one per color index value (0..3).
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] Each word packs the 6×3-bit pindirs sequence (18 bits used).
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] A couple of things worth deciding before we write the init:
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] • Q1 — pin mapping.* Each fifo needs a unique JMP pin. Are PUMP0..3 hard-mapped to fifo
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 0..3 (so SM0→GP2, SM1→GP3, SM2→GP4, SM3→GP5)?
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] • Q2 — preload semantics. The four words in each SM's "rxfifo" (txget) are the four
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] pulse trains for index 0..3 for that particular pump cycle. Do all four SMs hold the
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] same* four colors, or does each SM represent a different color palette / timing slot that the
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] colorpump sequences through?
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] • Q3 — refilling.* `rxfifo[y]` is non-destructive indexed read (doesn't pop), so once you
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] preload the 4 words they stay until you rewrite them. Are these per-frame, per-line, or
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] static-for-the-whole-runtime?
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] • Q4 — pin direction baseline.* Since the SM toggles `pindirs` and the actual pin levels
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] are presumably set elsewhere (held low?), confirm: the output pins are pre-driven low by SIO, and
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] the SM merely gates them by flipping pindirs to drive-low vs Hi-Z (open-collector style into the
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] resistor ladder)?
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] 
2026-05-11 20:43:04 [claude-opus-4-7] Which of these do you want to nail down first?
