2026-05-11 21:42:22 [simon@midnightblue.local] the colorpump needs to draw fixed number of pixels and then wait for next line, using irqactive line using irq
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] To make the `colorpump` draw a fixed number of pixels per line and wait for `vidbit` to signal the
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] start of the active video, we need to do three things:
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 1. Uncomment the IRQ in `vidbit.pio` so it fires at the start of the active line.
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 2. Rewrite `colorpump.pio` to wait for that IRQ, load a pixel counter for the line, and
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] loop exactly that many times.
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 3. Cycle-balance the `colorpump` branches so that regardless of which color is drawn, the
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] loop takes exactly 10 cycles (matching the 10-cycle pixel width of your `colorfifo` SMs).
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] Here is the updated PIO code and the C++ initialization to make it work.
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 1. Update `colorpump.pio`
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] We will use the `ISR` to hold the "pixels per line - 1" value (just like you did in `vidbit.pio`).
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] Every time the IRQ fires, we copy it to `Y` and count down.
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] ; colorpump.pio
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] ; outs 2 gpio pins for color index
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] ; pulses low 1 of 4 side set pins to trigger a colorfifo
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] ; waits for IRQ 0 to start the line, draws fixed pixels, then waits again
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] .program colorpump
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] .wrap_target
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] line_start:
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	wait 1 irq 0 clear   ; Wait for vidbit to signal active line, then clear flag
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	mov y, isr           ; Load pixel counter (e.g., 863) from ISR
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] pixel_loop:
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	out pins, 2          ; [1] 2 bits for color index
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	out x, 2             ; [1] 2 bits for FIFO select
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp x--, t3          ; [1]
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp x--, t2          ; [1]
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp x--, t1          ; [1]
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] t0:
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set pins, 14         ; [1]
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp done             ; [1]
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] t1:
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set pins, 13         ; [1]
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp done             ; [1]
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] t2:
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	nop                  ; [1] padding to balance cycles
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set pins, 11         ; [1]
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp done             ; [1]
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] t3:
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	nop [1]              ; [2] padding to balance cycles
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set pins, 7          ; [1]
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp done             ; [1]
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] done:
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	nop                  ; [1] (Pulse is low for 2 cycles: jmp + nop)
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set pins, 15         ; [1]
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp y--, pixel_loop  ; [1] Loop until Y hits 0
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] .wrap
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] • (Note: I carefully padded the branches with `nop`s. Because a `jmp` takes 1 cycle whether it is
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] taken or not, `t0` and `t1` take the same time to reach, `t2` is 1 cycle faster, and `t3` is 2
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] cycles faster. This padding guarantees exactly 10 cycles per pixel for every color).*
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 2. Update `vidbit.pio`
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] In `vidbit.pio`, find the commented-out IRQ line right before the `active:` label and uncomment it.
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] It should look like this:
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	; back porch = ~5.790 µs = 964 cycles (30*32+4)
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	pindirs, 0
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	pins, 1
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	y, BACKPORCH_WAIT32	;28
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] backporch:
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	y--,backporch [31]
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	irq	set 0               ; <-- UNCOMMENT THIS LINE
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	; active ≈ 51.904 µs = 8642 cycles (864×10+2)
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	mov	y,isr
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] active:
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	out	pindirs, 1 [8]
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	y--,active
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 3. Update `colorpump_init` in C++
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] Because `colorpump.pio` now relies on `mov y, isr` to know how many pixels to draw, we have to
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] preload the `ISR` register with the pixel count (864 pixels - 1 = 863) during initialization.
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] Add these three lines to `colorpumpinit` right before you call
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] `piosmsetenabled(pio, sm, true);`:
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	// ... existing colorpump config ...
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	pio_sm_init(pio, sm, offset6, &config6);
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	// Preload the colorpump's ISR with the active pixel count (864 - 1)
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	pio_sm_put_blocking(pio, sm, 863);
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	pio_sm_exec(pio, sm, pio_encode_pull(false, false));
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	pio_sm_exec(pio, sm, pio_encode_mov(pio_isr, pio_osr));
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	pio_sm_set_enabled(pio, sm, true);
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] How it works together now:
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 1. `vidbit` handles the HSYNC and backporch.
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 2. Right as `vidbit` starts outputting active video, it fires `irq 0`.
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 3. `colorpump` wakes up from `wait 1 irq 0 clear`, copies `863` into `Y`, and starts pumping
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] exactly 864 colors.
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 4. Because the loop is cycle-balanced to 10 cycles, `colorpump` stays perfectly locked in phase
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] with `vidbit` across the entire scanline.
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 5. Once `Y` hits 0, `colorpump` wraps back to the top and goes to sleep, ignoring the front porch
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] and sync periods until `vidbit` fires the IRQ on the next line.
2026-05-11 21:44:01 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] Your C++ updates in `vidbit.cpp` to preload the `ISR` with `863` are perfectly correct! That
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] successfully sets up the `colorpump` to count 864 pixels per line.
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] However, we need to take a close look at the `colorpump.pio` file. There is a sneaky logical bug in
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] how `jmp x--` works, and the cycle-balancing needs to be extremely precise to guarantee exactly 10
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] cycles per pixel across all 4 colors.
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] The `jmp x--` Bug
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] In PIO, `jmp x--, label` means: "If X is not 0, jump to the label. In either case, decrement
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] X."
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] If you cascade them like this:
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro]     jmp x--, t3
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro]     jmp x--, t2
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] If X is `0`, the first instruction evaluates `0 != 0` (False), so it does not jump, but it
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] still decrements X to `0xFFFFFFFF`. The second instruction then evaluates `0xFFFFFFFF != 0` (True),
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] and jumps to `t2`! This breaks the switch statement entirely.
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] The 10-Cycle Balanced Solution
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] To decode 2 bits in PIO, we have to use a combination of `jmp !x` and `jmp x--`. Because this
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] decoding takes a variable number of cycles depending on the value of X (X=3 takes longer to decode
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] than X=0), we must balance the paths using `nop` delays and inline the end of the loop so every
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] single path takes exactly 10 cycles.
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] Here is the corrected and perfectly balanced `colorpump.pio`:
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] ; colorpump.pio
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] ; outs 2 gpio pins for color index
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] ; pulses low 1 of 4 side set pins to trigger a colorfifo
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] ; waits for IRQ 0 to start the line, draws fixed pixels, then waits again
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] .program colorpump
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] .wrap_target
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	wait	1 irq 0 clear
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	mov	y, isr
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] pixel:
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	out	pins, 2        ; [1] Shift 2 bits to COLOR_I0,1
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	out	x, 2           ; [1] Shift 2 bits to X (Pump Select)
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	!x t0          ; [1] If X==0, jump to t0
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	x-- t1_chk     ; [1] X!=0, decrement X and check next
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] t1_chk:
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	!x t1          ; [1] If X==0 (was 1), jump to t1
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	x-- t2_chk     ; [1] X!=0, decrement X and check next
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] t2_chk:
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	!x t2          ; [1] If X==0 (was 2), jump to t2
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] t3: ; Reached in 5 cycles from 'jmp !x t0'
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	pins, 7        ; [1] Pulse PUMP3 low
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	pins, 15       ; [1] Return all pumps high
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	y--, pixel     ; [1] Loop (Total = 10 cycles)
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] t2: ; Reached in 5 cycles
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	pins, 11       ; [1] Pulse PUMP2 low
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	pins, 15       ; [1] Return all pumps high
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	y--, pixel     ; [1] Loop (Total = 10 cycles)
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] t1: ; Reached in 3 cycles
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	nop	[1]            ; [2] Delay to balance cycles
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	pins, 13       ; [1] Pulse PUMP1 low
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	pins, 15       ; [1] Return all pumps high
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	y--, pixel     ; [1] Loop (Total = 10 cycles)
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] t0: ; Reached in 1 cycle
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	nop	[3]            ; [4] Delay to balance cycles
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	pins, 14       ; [1] Pulse PUMP0 low
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	pins, 15       ; [1] Return all pumps high
2026-05-11 21:52:54 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	y--, pixel     ; [1] Loop (Total = 10 cycles)
