2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] I see you are trying to create a compact "fall-through" cascade to decode the 2 bits. It is a very
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] clever idea, but unfortunately, the PIO instruction set doesn't execute `jmp x--` the way you are
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] expecting it to.
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] In the PIO hardware, `jmp x--, label` evaluates as: "If X is greater than 0, jump to the
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] label."
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] If we trace your code, here is what happens:
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	out	x, 2          ; X becomes 0, 1, 2, or 3
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	!x, t3        ; If X == 0, it jumps to t3. (This works!)
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	x--, t2       ; If X > 0, it jumps to t2.
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	x--, t1       ; UNREACHABLE
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] t0:                   ; UNREACHABLE
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] Because 1, 2, and 3 are all greater than 0, the instruction `jmp x--, t2` will always jump
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] to `t2` for all three of those values. The execution will never reach `t1` or `t0`.
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] To decode 4 distinct values in PIO, you must test for zero, then decrement, then test for
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] zero again. Because this creates paths of different lengths, you also have to pad them with `nop`
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] delays so that every color takes exactly 10 cycles.
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] Here is the exact code you need for `colorpump.pio` to decode the 4 colors correctly and maintain
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] perfect 10-cycle video timing:
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] ; colorpump.pio
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] ; outs 2 gpio pins for color index
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] ; pulses low 1 of 4 side set pins to trigger a colorfifo
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] .program colorpump
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] .wrap_target
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	wait	1 irq 0 clear
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	mov	y, isr
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] pixel:
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	out	pins, 2        ; [1]
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	out	x, 2           ; [1]
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	!x t0          ; [1] If X==0, jump to t0
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	x-- check_1    ; [1] X was >0, decrement to check next
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] check_1:
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	!x t1          ; [1] If X==0 (was 1), jump to t1
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	x-- check_2    ; [1] X was >0, decrement to check next
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] check_2:
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	!x t2          ; [1] If X==0 (was 2), jump to t2
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] t3: ; Reached in 7 cycles (X=3)
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	pins, 7        ; [1]
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	pins, 15       ; [1]
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	y--, pixel     ; [1] -> Total 10 cycles
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] t2: ; Reached in 7 cycles (X=2)
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	pins, 11       ; [1]
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	pins, 15       ; [1]
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	y--, pixel     ; [1] -> Total 10 cycles
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] t1: ; Reached in 5 cycles (X=1)
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	nop	[1]            ; [2] Pad to balance timing
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	pins, 13       ; [1]
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	set	pins, 15       ; [1]
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 	jmp	y--, pixel     ; [1] -> Total 10 cycles
2026-05-11 22:09:59 [gemini-3.1-pro] 
