2026-05-14 17:49:13 [simon@midnightblue.local] i am worried that switching projects means history has huge context with both shares
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] You are right to be worried. The current code does not clear previous shared file content when
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] switching projects, so the context grows unbounded.
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] The problem
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] In `relay.ts`, when you execute `/project <key>` it calls `loadProject()`, which in turn calls
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] `setProject()`. That function updates `roha.sharedFiles` and `rohaSharePaths` to point to the new
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] project's shares, but it never removes the old shared file blobs from `rohaHistory`. The
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] history is a linear array — those image base64 strings and long text snippets from the prior
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] project remain, eating tokens.
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] Similarly, the `model` selection (`/model`) adds system messages like `"models under test include
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] deepseek-v4"` but does not discard prior file context.
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] Suggested fix
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] Add a new helper function that purges all user‑role messages that came from shared files
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] (identifiable by `name === "blob"`, `name === "content"`, or `name === "image"`) before loading the
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] new project. You can optionally also remove the corresponding `rohaSystem` hints that mention old
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] projects.
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] Here is a targeted patch for `relay.ts`:
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] // Add this function after resetHistory()
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] function removeSharedFileMessages() {
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4]     rohaHistory = rohaHistory.filter(item => {
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4]         // Remove any message that represents a file share
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4]         return !(item.role === "user" &&
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4]                  (item.name === "blob" || item.name === "content" || item.name === "image"));
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4]     });
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] }
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] Then modify `setProject()` to call it before switching, so the old file blobs are gone:
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] async function setProject(name, path) {
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4]     // Clear old shared file messages from history
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4]     removeSharedFileMessages();
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4]     // ... rest of existing logic ...
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4]     echo("[KEY] setProject", name, path);
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4]     const key = name;
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4]     // etc.
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] }
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] • Optional but recommended* – also trim any system messages about the old project:
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] function removeProjectSystemMessages(projectName) {
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4]     rohaHistory = rohaHistory.filter(item => {
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4]         return !(item.role === "system" &&
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4]                  item.content?.includes(`project: ${projectName}`));
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4]     });
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] }
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] Call that in `setProject` as well if you want a clean slate.
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] Additional consideration
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] If you want to keep the conversation content (user queries and model replies) but only
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] clear the file context, the filter above is sufficient. If you also want to keep the model's
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] awareness of the new project, you can re‑insert a fresh system message after the clear:
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] // After clearing old messages, add a new project context marker
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] rohaHistory.push({
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4]     role: "system",
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4]     title: "Fountain Tool Hint",
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4]     content: `Project: ${name} loaded. Feel free to call tag_slop to tag related items.`
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] });
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] Result
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] After this change, switching projects will:
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 1. Remove all previous file blobs from history.
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 2. Load the new project's share list.
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 3. Keep user‑model conversation (unless you want to reset that too – then call `resetHistory()`
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] before setting the project).
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] This keeps context size proportional to the active project only, solving the unbounded growth you
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] observed.
2026-05-14 17:49:25 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-14 17:51:23 [simon@midnightblue.local] i should just call the dropShares command before setting new one?
2026-05-14 17:51:36 [deepseek-v4] Your idea is a good start—calling `/drop` before switching projects will replace the shared file
2026-05-14 17:51:36 [deepseek-v4] content in history with a short placeholder, which significantly reduces token usage. However, it
2026-05-14 17:51:36 [deepseek-v4] does not remove the entries entirely; they remain as `{role:"user", name:"fountain",
2026-05-14 17:51:36 [deepseek-v4] content:"dropped share"}`. Those still consume a few tokens each and may clutter the context.
