2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] Thank you for sharing the vidbit project files. This is a substantial low-level video generator for
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] the RP2350 (Pico 2), targeting PAL 576i with a 166.5 MHz system clock. Here's my assessment:
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] Key Design Observations
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] - PIO pipeline architecture – The `pixelpump → onebit → threepin` chain provides a clean
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] separation: pixelpump handles line timing, onebit selects between two colour wave trains per pixel,
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] and threepin drives three tristate pins for component output. This modular approach allows reuse
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] and independent testing.
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] - DMA-driven continuous output – The main loop uses DMA channels to feed pixel data, chroma
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] bursts, and teletext data to PIO TX FIFOs. The `vid_field()` function configures DMA transfers per
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] field, and the main loop waits for DMA completion before triggering the next frame. This is
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] standard but well-executed.
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] - Interlaced vs progressive – The `LACE` ifdef enables interlaced output with separate
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] even/odd field buffers (`evenFrame`, `oddFrame`). The `vid_fieldi()` function sets different word
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] counts for each field. The teletext also alternates between even/odd line positions.
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] - Colour modulation – The `colorfifo.pio` and `colorpump.pio` files describe a scheme where
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] colour indexes (2 bits from pixel data) select one of four PIO state machines, each preloaded with
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] four unique 6-cycle pulse trains. The `colorpump` pulses a side-set pin low to trigger the selected
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] colourfifo. This allows up to 16 colours per pixel with minimal per-pixel overhead.
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] - Chroma subcarrier – The `chroma.pio` program appears to generate the PAL colour burst and
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] modulated chrominance signal using a DMA ring buffer with precomputed sine wave patterns. The PIO's
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] `clkdiv` is set to 2.3471 to achieve the correct subcarrier frequency (approx 4.43 MHz from 166.5
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] MHz). The `initChroma()` function builds a 128-word table alternating even/odd field phases.
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] - Teletext (WST) – Full implementation of World System Teletext using Hamming 8/4 encoding
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] and row-based packet construction. The `wstEven`/`wstOdd` arrays are built per field, with variable
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] line positions due to different field lengths (309 vs 310 lines). The teletext DMA is triggered
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] independently of the video DMA, but both run on the same PIO machine.
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] - Resistor network mixing – The `vidbit.md` and `vidbit.h` documents show multiple output
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] configurations: composite video using LUMA + CHROMA resistors, component video using Y/Pb/Pr
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] resistors, and direct greyscale output. The circuit uses standard resistor summing networks with 75
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] Ω termination.
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] - Conditional compilation – The code uses `#ifdef COLOR`, `#ifdef GREY`, `#ifdef CHROMA`,
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] `#ifdef WST`, `#ifdef LACE` to select features. This is necessary for the small PIO memory, but
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] creates multiple binary variants. Consider runtime configuration or at least clearer documentation
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] of valid combinations.
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] - PS/2 and I2S – Separate state machines for keyboard input and audio output are
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] initialized but the audio output loop is commented out (`#ifdef STREAM_AUDIO`). The PS/2 reading is
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] minimal.
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] Potential Issues or Improvements
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 1. PIO program address space – The code attempts to load `vidbit`, `wst`, `chroma`,
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] `greyline`, `onebit`, `threepin`, plus PS/2 and I2S programs onto PIO0 and PIO1. The RP2350 has 8
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] state machines across two PIO blocks, but instruction memory per block is limited (typically 128
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] instructions per block). Ensure total programs fit without overlap.
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 2. Interlace alignment – The `initFramei()` and `initFrame()` functions are not shown. The
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] field counter `field` increments continuously, but the PAL standard requires the odd field to start
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] half a line later. The DMA triggers must account for this offset. The current code uses
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] `drawFramei(field)` which presumably handles field parity.
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 3. Timing jitter – The main loop polls `dmachannelis_busy()`. If the CPU is delayed
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] by USB CDC processing, the DMA restart may be late, causing visible jitter. Consider using PIO IRQ
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] handlers or a timer IRQ to restart DMA more deterministically.
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 4. Teletext line placement – The code inserts teletext data on lines 7..22, but the PAL
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] blanking interval varies. Lines 6-22 and 318-335 are typical for teletext, but the current
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] hardcoded offsets (skip1=7) may need adjustment if field length changes.
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 5. Colour indexing – The `colorfifo` uses `mov y, pins` to read the colour index from GPIO
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] pins, implying the index is provided externally (likely from `colorpump.pio`). The `colorpump` sets
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] these pins via `out pins, 2`. This introduces a timing dependency across PIO machines; ensure the
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] index is stable before the fifo reads it.
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 6. Power and termination – The resistor values in `vidbit.h` (e.g., 120 Ω + 150 Ω + 330 Ω +
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 100 Ω) produce specific voltage levels for luma and chroma. Verify against PAL composite voltage
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] specs (0–0.7 V for luma, ±0.3 V for chroma). The 3.3 V supply divided by these resistors may exceed
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] the 0.7 V target.
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] Overall Impression
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] This is a well-structured, low-level project that demonstrates deep understanding of RP2350 PIO and
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] DMA capabilities. The modular PIO pipeline and conditional compilation make it adaptable for
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] different video standards and feature sets. The inclusion of teletext and colour modulation is
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] particularly interesting. The main challenges are ensuring deterministic timing and fitting all PIO
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] programs into memory. I'd recommend adding runtime configuration over BINARY GPIO or serial
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] commands rather than compile-time only options.
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] If you'd like me to examine a specific component in more detail (e.g., the chroma generation, the
2026-05-17 18:11:44 [deepseek-v4] interlacing logic, or the PS/2 driver), just let me know.
