2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] Thank you for the detailed timing analysis. I'll verify the porch durations in `vidbit.pio` against
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] the PAL 576i line timing (166.5 MHz, 10656 cycles per line).
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] Line total check
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] The line loop executes:
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] 1. HSYNC – `set` (2 cycles) + `set y, 26` (1) + `jmp y--, hsync [28]` loop of 26 iterations
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] × 29 cycles/iteration = 754 → sum 757 cycles
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] 2. Back porch – `set pindirs,0` (1) + `set pins,1` (1) + `set y, 26` (1) + loop 26 × 32 =
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] 832 → sum 835 cycles
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] 3. Active video – `mov y, isr` (1) + loop 864 × 10 = 8640 → sum 8641 cycles
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] (comment says 8642, but the first `out pindirs,1` is inside the loop, so 8641 is correct)
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] 4. Front porch – `set pindirs,0` (1) + `set y, 9` (1) + loop 9 × 32 = 288 → sum 290
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] cycles
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] 5. Final jump – `jmp x--, line [12]` = 13 cycles
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] • Total line = 757 + 835 + 8641 + 290 + 13 = 10536 cycles – 120 cycles
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] short* of the required 10656.
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] Comment vs. actual cycles
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] ╭───────────────┬────────────────────┬───────────────────┬──────────────╮
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] │  Section      │  Comment (cycles)  │  Actual (cycles)  │  Difference  │
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] ├───────────────┼────────────────────┼───────────────────┼──────────────┤
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] │  HSYNC        │  786 (27×29+3)     │  757 (26×29+3)    │  –29         │
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] │  Back porch   │  964 (30×32+4)     │  835 (26×32+3)    │  –129        │
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] │  Active       │  8642 (864×10+2)   │  8641             │  –1          │
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] │  Front porch  │  258 (8×32+2)      │  290 (9×32+2)     │  +32         │
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] │  Final jmp    │  13 (1+12)         │  13               │  0           │
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] ╰───────────────┴────────────────────┴───────────────────┴──────────────╯
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] Root cause
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] The `HSYNCWAIT29`, `BACKPORCHWAIT32`, and `FRONTPORCH_WAIT32` defines are
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] incorrect. They should be:
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] - `HSYNC_WAIT29` = 27 (to give 27 × 29 = 783 cycles + 3 setup = 786)
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] - `BACKPORCH_WAIT32` = 30 (to give 30 × 32 = 960 + 4 setup = 964)
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] - `FRONTPORCH_WAIT32` = 8 (to give 8 × 32 = 256 + 2 setup = 258)
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] With these corrections:
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] - HSYNC = 786
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] - Back porch = 964
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] - Active = 8641 (unchanged, but comment says 8642 – likely off-by-one in the comment; actual active
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] loop is 8641 cycles, which is acceptable)
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] - Front porch = 258
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] - Final jmp = 13
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] • Sum = 786 + 964 + 8641 + 258 + 13 = 10662 cycles – still 6 cycles over* the
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] required 10656.
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] Remaining discrepancy
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] The overshoot of 6 cycles can be absorbed by:
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] - Reducing the `active` loop count by 1 (863 iterations → 8630 cycles, total 10652) and adding 4
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] more cycles elsewhere, or
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] - Adjusting the final `jmp` delay from 12 to 6 (7 cycles total) and keeping active at 864
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] iterations → 10656 exactly.
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] Given that the active video line is typically 864 pixels, I recommend reducing the final JMP
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] delay to `[6]` (7 cycles), which trims the line total by exactly 6 cycles to 10656. This
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] preserves the 864-pixel active period.
2026-05-17 18:38:23 [deepseek-v4] 
