2026-05-18 20:01:20 [deepseek-v4] The HSYNC loop uses:
2026-05-18 20:01:20 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-18 20:01:20 [deepseek-v4] HSYNC_WAIT29 = 26
2026-05-18 20:01:20 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-18 20:01:20 [deepseek-v4] With the delay `[28]`, each iteration takes 29 cycles (`28+1`). The loop body is:
2026-05-18 20:01:20 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-18 20:01:20 [deepseek-v4] set y, HSYNC_WAIT29   ; 1 cycle
2026-05-18 20:01:20 [deepseek-v4] jmp y--, hsync [28]   ; 1 cycle + delay
2026-05-18 20:01:20 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-18 20:01:20 [deepseek-v4] When `y` starts at 26, the loop runs exactly 26 times? Let’s trace:
2026-05-18 20:01:20 [deepseek-v4] - y=26 → condition true, jump taken, y becomes 25 → 29 cycles.
2026-05-18 20:01:20 [deepseek-v4] - …
2026-05-18 20:01:20 [deepseek-v4] - y=1 → true, jump, y=0 → 29 cycles.
2026-05-18 20:01:20 [deepseek-v4] - y=0 → condition false, no jump, fall through → 29 cycles (delay still applies).
2026-05-18 20:01:20 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-18 20:01:20 [deepseek-v4] Total cycles: 27 iterations × 29 = 783 cycles, plus the initial `set` (1 cycle) = 784
2026-05-18 20:01:20 [deepseek-v4] cycles.
