2026-05-19 18:54:06 [deepseek-v4] ### 4. vidbit.pio vsync
2026-05-19 18:54:06 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-19 18:54:06 [deepseek-v4] The vsync section at the top reads `OUT x,32` then uses a pulse train of 32 pulses. This overwrites the line counter? The comment says fifo[0] = vsync pulsetrain edge-width counter = 32-1, [1..32] = pulse widths. This is quite involved. For 576i, VSYNC is 5 lines long? Actually PAL uses 5 equalising pulses and 5 vsync pulses per field. Your approach seems to generate arbitrary pulse widths. That’s flexible but adds complexity. Make sure the VSYNC timing fits within the 10656 cycle line budget.
