2026-05-19 18:54:06 [deepseek-v4] ### 5. activeline.pio
2026-05-19 18:54:06 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-19 18:54:06 [deepseek-v4] This is a minimal loop that outputs 2 bits per pixel at 10 cycles per pixel. It waits on IRQ6 from vidbit. However, vidbit.pio sets `irq next clear 6` at the end of active, so the timing may not align. Also note that activeline outputs `out pins,2` but the `out` base must be set to the first of those two pins. This will operate without the colour resolution of the threepin approach.
