2026-05-22 20:58:46 [deepseek-v4] The shared files describe vidbit, a PAL video generator for the RP2350 (Pico2) using PIO
2026-05-22 20:58:46 [deepseek-v4] state machines and resistor-ladder DACs. This is a non-trivial project that demonstrates advanced
2026-05-22 20:58:46 [deepseek-v4] use of the RP2350's PIO capabilities, including:
2026-05-22 20:58:46 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-22 20:58:46 [deepseek-v4] - 166.5 MHz system clock – chosen to yield exactly 10 cycles per pixel at PAL line rate
2026-05-22 20:58:46 [deepseek-v4] (64 µs → 10 656 cycles, 864 pixels → 10 cycles/pixel).
2026-05-22 20:58:46 [deepseek-v4] - Multiple PIO programs working in a pipeline:
2026-05-22 20:58:46 [deepseek-v4]   - `vidbit.pio` – generates HSYNC, VSYNC, back/front porch, and triggers an IRQ for the active
2026-05-22 20:58:46 [deepseek-v4] video line.
2026-05-22 20:58:46 [deepseek-v4]   - `onebit.pio` / `threepin.pio` – implement a 1‑bit pixel stream with two colour waveforms, then
2026-05-22 20:58:46 [deepseek-v4] drive three tristate pins (Y, Pb, Pr) per pixel.
2026-05-22 20:58:46 [deepseek-v4]   - `colorpump.pio` / `colorfifo.pio` – pump colour words from a lookup table (indexed via
2026-05-22 20:58:46 [deepseek-v4] `FJOIN_RX_GET`) into the output FIFOs.
2026-05-22 20:58:46 [deepseek-v4] - 576i interlaced and 288p progressive modes – with two separate frame buffers
2026-05-22 20:58:46 [deepseek-v4] (`evenFrame`, `oddFrame`).
2026-05-22 20:58:46 [deepseek-v4] - World System Teletext (WST) overlay – uses Hamming(8,4) encoded packets on lines 7‑22.
2026-05-22 20:58:46 [deepseek-v4] - Chroma subcarrier – separate PIO state machine generating a PAL burst (via `chroma.pio`)
2026-05-22 20:58:46 [deepseek-v4] at ~4.43 MHz.
2026-05-22 20:58:46 [deepseek-v4] - Audio – I2S output from a simple noise/fuzz generator.
2026-05-22 20:58:46 [deepseek-v4] - PS/2 keyboard/mouse input – via two additional state machines.
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] - Flash filesystem – LittleFS integrated.
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] - USB CDC interactive console – for runtime commands and status reporting.
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] What is new or different?
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] 1. PIO state machine cascade – Three SMs are chained (pixelpump → onebit → threepin) to
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] separate pixel generation, colour mapping, and physical pin driving. This is a clean, modular
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] design that leverages the shallow FIFOs efficiently.
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] 2. Using `FJOIN_RX_GET` for colour lookup tables – The `colorfifo.pio` program reads
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] indexed RX FIFO entries (via `mov osr, rxfifo[y]`) to select colour words on a per‑pixel basis.
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] This is a relatively new RP2350 feature (absent on RP2040) and is used here for real‑time palette
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] access.
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] 3. Cycle‑exact PAL timing – The `vidbit.pio` program uses carefully chosen delay values and
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] `jmp`/`irq` to stay within 10 656 cycles per line. The use of `irq next set 6` to synchronise the
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] active‑line state machine is a clever cross‑PIO synchronisation technique.
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] 4. Monobit rendering with 2‑bit colour – The `monobit.cpp` draws characters and shapes into
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] a bit‑plane using two bits per pixel (for 4 colour levels from resistor weights). The `flipBits2`
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] function packs 2‑bit pixel chunks into 32‑bit words for the PIO to shift out.
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] 5. Teletext generator – Implementing WST in software and feeding pre‑encoded packets into
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] the PIO is unusual; typically teletext is a hardware block. The Hamming code tables are
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] pre‑computed and the packet format mimics real teletext data.
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] 6. Resource‑efficient use of DMA – Multiple DMA channels handle frame buffers, colour
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] tables, teletext packets, and S/PDIF audio, all chained at field rate. The ring‑buffer DMA for
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] chroma (`chroma_dma_init` with `channel_config_set_ring`) is a nice touch for continuous burst
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] generation.
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] Potential concerns / suggestions
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] 
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] - Resistor DAC values – The schematics show 3.3 V straight into 120 Ω (composite) or 80 Ω
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] (component). This exceeds the standard 75 Ω termination and may cause reflections or non‑standard
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] video levels. A proper video DAC would use a more precise resistor network (e.g., R‑2R) or a
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] dedicated video buffer.
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] - Interrupt synchronisation – The `wait 1 irq 6` in `activeline.pio` may suffer race
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] conditions if the `vidbit` SM fires the IRQ too early or late. Consider adding a `nop` or a small
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] delay to guarantee the FIFO is ready.
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] - FIFO depth – With 864 pixels per line and a 4‑entry FIFO, the CPU/DMA must keep the FIFO
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] fed. The current design uses a field‑long DMA transfer, which works, but a double‑buffered approach
2026-05-22 20:58:47 [deepseek-v4] (ping‑pong) would reduce latency.
