2026-05-30 16:38:49 [claude-opus-4-8]  ꔀ nitrologic Relay 1.8.7 ⛲  claude-opus-4-8 A\ 🪠 🧊 $0.762 344.0KB 34.75s
2026-05-30 16:38:49 [claude-opus-4-8] Quite a bundle. The VIDBIT video generator is the heart of it and it's a lovely bit of work —
2026-05-30 16:38:49 [claude-opus-4-8] squeezing PAL 576i and 288p out of PIO state machines with resistor-ladder DACs. A few things stood
2026-05-30 16:38:49 [claude-opus-4-8] out as new to me:
2026-05-30 16:38:49 [claude-opus-4-8] 
2026-05-30 16:38:49 [claude-opus-4-8] The `vidbit.pio` timing comments are doing the heavy lifting. The sync structure encoded as FIFO
2026-05-30 16:38:49 [claude-opus-4-8] words — `[0]` vsync edge count, then `[1..n]` pulse widths, then linecounter and pixelcounter — is
2026-05-30 16:38:49 [claude-opus-4-8] a neat way to push the entire field timing through DMA without CPU intervention. The `irq next set
2026-05-30 16:38:49 [claude-opus-4-8] 6` / `clear 6` bracketing the active region is presumably how you'd hand off to an active-line
2026-05-30 16:38:49 [claude-opus-4-8] pumper on the next PIO block.
2026-05-30 16:38:49 [claude-opus-4-8] 
2026-05-30 16:38:49 [claude-opus-4-8] The 2-bits-per-pixel move in `monobit.h` (`bitsPerPixel=2`, `lineWords=27*2`) with the `ditherMem`
2026-05-30 16:38:49 [claude-opus-4-8] ordered-dither patterns is a clean way to get apparent greys out of a fundamentally binary signal.
2026-05-30 16:38:49 [claude-opus-4-8] The `flipBits16` expansion doubling each bit is tidy.
2026-05-30 16:38:49 [claude-opus-4-8] 
2026-05-30 16:38:49 [claude-opus-4-8] The colour path is the most experimental-looking corner — `make_color_train` packing Y/Pb/Pr PDM
2026-05-30 16:38:49 [claude-opus-4-8] into a 3-lane bit train, fed through `colorpump` → `colorfifo` on pio2. That
2026-05-30 16:38:49 [claude-opus-4-8] `0b0'000'...'111'110'011'001'111` binary grouping in the test trains is very readable.
2026-05-30 16:38:49 [claude-opus-4-8] 
2026-05-30 16:38:49 [claude-opus-4-8] One thing I noticed: `vidbit.md` flags "864 pixels is too many pixels" under INVESTIGATE,
2026-05-30 16:38:49 [claude-opus-4-8] and the `mode` string in `vidbit2350.cpp` now says `<VIDBIT MICROPAL 77>`. Is the micropal
2026-05-30 16:38:49 [claude-opus-4-8] direction about dropping the active pixel count to ease the PIO/DMA bandwidth?
2026-05-30 16:38:49 [claude-opus-4-8] 
